# Life is Strange: Double Exposure (Unreal Engine 5, ships the D3D12 Agility SDK)
# DX12 on D3DMetal hangs in the main menu: the game thread spins around
# DXGIAdapter::QueryVideoMemoryInfo. DX11 on DXMT reaches the game and plays at ~45 fps
# (menus still slow). Tested 2026-10-10 on an M4 with 16 GB, Steam build 1788652215.
# Menu findings: the game defaults to exclusive fullscreen at the panel's native 2560x1664.
# Without Retina mode Wine draws that 1:1 into the top-left corner (the "messed up" menu);
# WOVEN_RETINA=1 fixes the layout. The title scene costs ~337 ms GPU per frame at native
# resolution (Metal HUD: ~3 fps), so the slow menu is GPU load, not a driver stall.
# Being tested: Retina mode plus a lower in-game resolution scale.
CX_GRAPHICS_BACKEND=dxmt
WOVEN_GAME_ARGS=-dx11
